Package: riprvis
Title: Interactive Visualisations for Reverse Information Projections
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Floyd", "Everest", , "me@floydeverest.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Interactive 'htmlwidgets' visualisations of reverse information
    projection (RIPr) fits and their branch-and-bound certification, as
    computed by the 'ripr' package for multinomial families on the
    two-simplex. Three widgets cover the pipeline: the problem (the null
    region and the alternative's support), the fit (the Bernstein field
    G(theta) = E[Q/P] over the simplex with per-step diagnostics), and the
    certification (the evolving cell partition, enclosure window and search
    tree). Each widget accepts a plain-list payload, so the package renders
    saved results without 'ripr' installed; companion data helpers build the
    payloads directly from 'ripr' objects.
